WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.363 --> 00:00:03.030
(lapping waves)

00:00:19.683 --> 00:00:21.359
- Hey, what's goin' on?

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:23.288
Welcome to Brooklyn, New York.

00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:25.279
It's not the greatest place in the world,

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:28.351
but it's where we live for now.

00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:31.686
I'm planning on movin' to Saint Martin.

00:00:31.686 --> 00:00:33.738
I'm just used to home, which is New York,

00:00:33.738 --> 00:00:35.632
but I definitely wanna move back out

00:00:35.632 --> 00:00:39.632
to the Caribbean Islands,
which is my, you know, real home.

00:00:41.203 --> 00:00:43.734
So, nothing against America,
but I'm just used to, like

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:47.832
the natural food, the natural
water, the natural air.

00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:48.891
Everything is cleaner down there.

00:00:48.891 --> 00:00:51.221
The water's actually blue, it's not green.

00:00:51.221 --> 00:00:54.574
No offense to Orchard Beach, but it is.

00:00:54.574 --> 00:00:56.917
And yeah, you don't have grocery
stores and stuff like that,

00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:59.020
that's open 24 hours,
but the crime is down.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.853
So, it's not that bad.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:08.543
Probably the only thing good in the hood.

00:01:08.543 --> 00:01:10.914
Vitamin Water, where's
our endorsement deal?

00:01:10.914 --> 00:01:14.032
We've been pushin' you
guys for like 10 years now.

00:01:14.032 --> 00:01:17.115
(background talking)

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:25.027
Alright, y’all.

00:01:26.448 --> 00:01:27.432
- Nah.

00:01:27.432 --> 00:01:28.599
- Video games.

00:01:29.515 --> 00:01:30.348
- Yeah.

00:01:30.515 --> 00:01:32.348
- All right, get me on a game.
I’m like CJ over San Andreas.

00:01:33.384 --> 00:01:35.467
(laughs)

00:01:39.158 --> 00:01:42.844
The good news is, in the hood as long as

00:01:42.844 --> 00:01:45.556
you're cool with the
people nobody bothers you.

00:01:45.556 --> 00:01:46.746
So, and they can tell whether or not

00:01:46.746 --> 00:01:48.475
you're from the hood or not.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.982
Like, I’m endangering the cameraman, everybody,

00:01:50.982 --> 00:01:53.648
but as long as he's with me he's alright.

00:01:53.648 --> 00:01:57.139
We understand the environment
so we know the dos and don'ts

00:01:57.139 --> 00:02:00.750
It's like you get this heightened
sense of how to avoid the danger,

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.673
and stay away from certain people.

00:02:02.673 --> 00:02:03.988
We just do our thing here.

00:02:03.988 --> 00:02:05.962
We just live here.

00:02:05.962 --> 00:02:07.200
We don't hang out here in Brooklyn.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.412
We wanna hang out we go into Manhattan.

00:02:09.412 --> 00:02:12.166
Blah, blah, blah, we live in the ghetto.

00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:13.566
We're not a part of it.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.566
(music)

00:02:22.596 --> 00:02:24.686
It's funny, the world's greatest gamer’s

00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:26.436
house is in this apartment.

00:02:32.677 --> 00:02:33.927
That's my room.

00:02:37.477 --> 00:02:38.702
- Excuse me?

00:02:38.702 --> 00:02:40.102
(all talking)

00:02:40.202 --> 00:02:43.202
I’m not even going to use the 
exercise to elaborate on that.

00:02:44.102 --> 00:02:49.102
I’m not going to use my carbon dioxide 
to elaborate on a stupid statement

00:02:49.991 --> 00:02:50.824
That's stupid, that statement was stupid.

00:02:50.824 --> 00:02:52.641
(all talking)

00:02:52.641 --> 00:02:54.724
I'm gonna let you rock on that, 
I’m gonna let you rock.
You’re Empire, I’m gonna let you get by.

00:02:58.126 --> 00:03:01.949
- It's Saturday, so we can usually
have all the members of the Empire

00:03:01.949 --> 00:03:06.116
come over and, pretty much, run
sessions, Marvel, Street Fighter.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.029
I remember these guys
when they were like 15.

00:03:10.029 --> 00:03:13.089
Now these guys are like
in their late 20s, and stuff like that,

00:03:13.089 --> 00:03:14.378
and they're all world champions.

00:03:14.802 --> 00:03:16.702
- That’s zero, frustration is setting in!

00:03:17.102 --> 00:03:18.602
- Nah, I’m not frustrated.

00:03:18.737 --> 00:03:20.628
If I’m frustrated, I just wanna play.

00:03:20.628 --> 00:03:25.246
I'm not mad, I'm just
tryin' to figure it out.

00:03:25.246 --> 00:03:27.592
- Players like me, I came from Jersey.

00:03:27.592 --> 00:03:29.766
So, this is a lot further for me,

00:03:29.766 --> 00:03:31.569
but when I come down
here this is what we do.

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:34.602
We play, we, I guess, do a think tank.

00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:37.282
We try to figure out the 
best way to be the best

00:03:37.282 --> 00:03:39.408
at the games that we play.

00:03:39.408 --> 00:03:42.151
So, with that in mind,
we require each other.

00:03:42.151 --> 00:03:45.401
It's like we couldn't do it on our own.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:52.169
- I, uh, met TriForce
through my best friend Jaron

00:03:52.169 --> 00:03:53.252
16 years ago.

00:03:57.726 --> 00:04:00.560
I didn't know someone
could play so many games,

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.316
and beat so many games.

00:04:02.316 --> 00:04:04.202
In the house there's also
a lot of other players,

00:04:04.202 --> 00:04:05.399
like Claymore.

00:04:05.399 --> 00:04:09.566
They all were really good
at different types of games.

00:04:10.754 --> 00:04:12.840
- Before I met TriForce
I just didn't know that

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.666
somebody could own over a thousand
games, physical games.

00:04:15.666 --> 00:04:17.921
This was before, like, 
a lot of these systems.

00:04:17.921 --> 00:04:20.754
This was like during SNES, Genesis, 64.

00:04:23.613 --> 00:04:25.044
- The most documented tournament wins

00:04:25.044 --> 00:04:28.689
for a gaming team is 1,111
achieved by Empire Arcadia,

00:04:28.689 --> 00:04:31.521
members of whom have
competed in live gaming

00:04:31.521 --> 00:04:34.556
tournaments, online competitions
and world record attempts,

00:04:34.556 --> 00:04:37.389
and we been doing this since 2003.

00:04:40.008 --> 00:04:41.443
How many people can actually
say their organization

00:04:41.443 --> 00:04:44.605
has over 20 something players

00:04:44.605 --> 00:04:46.691
in Guinness Book of World Record.

00:04:46.691 --> 00:04:47.524
Only one.

00:04:48.726 --> 00:04:51.846
(gaming sounds)

00:04:51.846 --> 00:04:54.545
- You can imagine I was
like seven, eight years old,

00:04:54.545 --> 00:04:57.162
and I was running around
the Bronx with my friends

00:04:57.162 --> 00:04:59.573
going to arcade to arcade
playing the latest games

00:04:59.573 --> 00:05:02.572
trying to get high scores.

00:05:02.572 --> 00:05:05.527
And then, you know, I got
older, I got married,

00:05:05.527 --> 00:05:07.095
and my wife was like,
"What are you gonna do?

00:05:07.095 --> 00:05:08.240
Do this forever?"

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.048
And I was like, "Pretty much.",

00:05:10.048 --> 00:05:12.464
and she was like, "Well it
better put food on the table."

00:05:12.464 --> 00:05:15.214
So that's when I
incorporated it into a business.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.214
(music)

